    ├── Used APIs  : command, argument, option, version_option, echo, File, Path, format_filename
    ├── Pitfalls   : Typer uses type hints for parameter declaration instead of decorators, requiring rewrite of all @click decorators;
    │   click.File and click.Path become typer.FileBinaryRead and typer.Path with different semantics; click.format_filename has no 
    │   direct equivalent; would need custom implementation or use os.path.basename; Typer's echo is typer.echo (same function, 
    │   re-exported from Click); Migration is not drop-in; requires restructuring CLI definition
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── Typer is built on top of Click and provides a modern, type-hint-based API that can replace Click for CLI definition. The code 
        uses Click decorators (@click.command, @click.argument, @click.option) and utilities (click.echo, click.File, click.Path, 
        click.format_filename, click.version_option) which have direct equivalents in Typer. Typer would require rewriting decorators 
        to use type hints (e.g., `infile: typer.FileBinaryRead = typer.Argument(None)` instead of `@click.argument('infile', 
        type=click.File('rb'), required=False)`), but the functional role is identical.

