    └── PyQt5, PySide6, and PyQt6 are all Qt bindings for Python with nearly identical APIs. The code uses standard Qt widgets, 
        layouts, and dialogs that exist across all three. PySide6 (LGPL) and PyQt6 (GPL/commercial) are the modern maintained versions;
        PyQt5 is end-of-life. Migration between them typically requires only import statement changes and minor enum namespace 
        adjustments (e.g., Qt.Horizontal -> Qt.Orientation.Horizontal in PyQt6/PySide6).

